`callback_on_step_end` builds its kwargs with one `locals()` call per requested
tensor name, per denoising step; each call materialises the whole ~45-entry
frame dictionary of `WanPipeline.__call__`.  Measured (out/videogen_more_cb,
region `callback_step`, 5.4% irregular):

    callback_step = 14,019.5*ninputs + 0.00755*numel + 10,873

with the per-name coefficient made of PyDict_Contains (2,436), PyDict_SetItem
(2,044), PyDict_Update (1,850), PyObject_SetItem (1,469) -- the frame snapshot,
not the values.  The diffusers default is three names, so 42k instructions per
step to read three variables that are in scope.  Hoisting the call leaves one
snapshot per step; the dict that reaches the callback is the same.

--- a/src/diffusers/pipelines/wan/pipeline_wan.py
+++ b/src/diffusers/pipelines/wan/pipeline_wan.py
@@ -636,9 +636,12 @@
                 if callback_on_step_end is not None:
+                    # `locals()` materialises the whole frame dict; it used to be
+                    # called once per requested name, per step.
+                    step_locals = locals()
                     callback_kwargs = {}
                     for k in callback_on_step_end_tensor_inputs:
-                        callback_kwargs[k] = locals()[k]
+                        callback_kwargs[k] = step_locals[k]
                     callback_outputs = callback_on_step_end(self, i, t, callback_kwargs)
